    "intro_html":  "Gai pad med mamuang is Thai cashew chicken, and the thing that makes it different from every Chinese cashew dish is the seasoning: fish sauce instead of just soy, and a lot more of it. Peppers and onion stay crunchy, the cashews get toasted first so they stay crisp instead of going soft, and the sauce is thin and salty rather than thick and gloppy. Each bowl comes in at \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
